1. A method for producing an ion exchange membrane for alkali chloride electrolysis, comprising:

- providing a fluorinated polymer precursor membrane comprising a sulfonic-acid-type layer and a carboxylic-acid-type layer;
- the carboxylic-acid-type layer containing fluorinated polymer structural units having carboxylic acid groups or groups convertible thereto in an amount of 10.0 to 15.0 mol% based on all structural units of the fluorinated polymer;
- contacting the precursor membrane with an aqueous alkaline treatment liquid containing an organic solvent at a concentration of 5 to 40 mass%; and
- carrying out the treatment at 40 to 95°C to convert the precursor functional groups to ion-exchange groups,

thereby obtaining an alkali chloride electrolysis ion exchange membrane having high current efficiency, reduced membrane-property variation, and improved alkali resistance.
